   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "An Introduction to Terpenes: What They Are and Why They Matter"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>When shopping for cannabis at our Wellfleet dispensary, you’ve probably noticed product descriptions mentioning words like <b>“myrcene,” “limonene,”</b> or <b>“caryophyllene.”</b> These aren’t just fancy terms—they’re <b>terpenes</b>, and they play a major role in how cannabis affects your mind and body.</p><p>Let’s break down what terpenes are, how they influence your experience, and why they’re worth paying attention to when choosing cannabis products.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "What Are Terpenes?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p><b>Terpenes</b> are naturally occurring aromatic compounds found in many plants—including cannabis. They’re responsible for the distinctive scents and flavors in everything from lavender to citrus to pine.</p><p>In cannabis, terpenes do more than smell good—they also help shape the <b>overall effects</b> of each strain. That calming indica or energizing sativa? Terpenes are a big part of the reason why they feel different.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "What is The Entourage Effect?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Terpenes don’t work alone—they interact with cannabinoids like <b>THC</b> and <b>CBD</b> to create what scientists call the <b>entourage effect</b>. This means that the combination of compounds works together synergistically, enhancing the potential therapeutic effects of cannabis.</p><p>For example, a strain high in both <b>limonene</b> and <b>THC</b> may feel more uplifting than a strain with the same THC level but different terpenes.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "What are the most common Cannabis Terpenes?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Here are a few of the most common terpenes found in cannabis and their potential effects:</p><ul><li><p><b>Myrcene</b> – Earthy, musky scent. Known for relaxing, sedative effects.</p></li><li><p><b>Limonene</b> – Citrus aroma. Uplifting and mood-boosting.</p></li><li><p><b>Caryophyllene</b> – Peppery or spicy smell. Anti-inflammatory and may help with pain.</p></li><li><p><b>Pinene</b> – Piney aroma. Promotes alertness and focus.</p></li><li><p><b>Linalool</b> – Floral scent. Calming and may ease anxiety or stress.</p></li></ul>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Why Do Terpenes Matter When Choosing Cannabis?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>At <b>Cape Cod Cannabis</b>, we believe the best cannabis experience comes from understanding what you’re putting into your body. Instead of choosing based solely on <b>THC percentage</b>, consider terpene content and how you want to feel.</p><p>Looking for deep relaxation after a day on the beach? Try a strain high in <b>myrcene</b>. Need focus and energy before a hike in the Cape Cod National Seashore? A <b>limonene</b>-rich sativa might be the move.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Shop by Terpene at Cape Cod Cannabis"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Whether you’re new to cannabis or a seasoned enthusiast, our team in <b>Wellfleet, MA</b> is here to help you explore strains and products that align with your goals—<b>flavor, effect, and experience</b>.</p><p>Browse our menu <a href=\"/menu/\">online here</a> or stop by to chat with one of our knowledgeable budtenders about terpene-rich flower, vapes, and edibles.</p><p>For more information please <a href=\"/terpene-cannabinoid-guide/\">visit our Terpene &amp; Cannabinoid Guide</a>.</p><p>—</p><p>#WhatAreTerpenes #TerpeneBenefits #CannabisEducation #CapeCodCannabis #EntourageEffect</p>"
    }
   ]
  },
